# Decurion's walls. A piece of work that changes any of these waits for the
# owner to look at it, even when the checker passes it. The hub reads this
# list from the commit the work started from, so the work cannot change it
# for itself. How patterns work: crates/decurion-hub/src/protected.rs.

# The sealed box agents run in: how the runner starts each container, what it
# may reach and which files it can see.
crates/decurion-runner/src/

# The gate: the only way out to the internet from inside a box.
crates/decurion-gate/

# The worker images and their settings, including the tools an agent gets
# (mcp.json) and the cloud worker's firewall (cloud/walls.sh).
docker/

# The vault that keeps apps' test keys locked.
crates/decurion-vault/

# Money and limits: the spending cap, Max account limits and usage meters.
crates/decurion-hub/src/spend.rs
crates/decurion-hub/src/limits.rs
crates/decurion-hub/src/usage.rs

# Phone notifications: what leaves the hub for push services, and the key
# that signs it.
crates/decurion-hub/src/push.rs

# Credentials: handing a run its one credential, and apps' test keys.
crates/decurion-hub/src/secrets.rs
crates/decurion-hub/src/test_keys.rs

# This hold itself: how the hub decides what is protected, where the check
# runs when a piece finishes, and the helpers' tool limits.
crates/decurion-hub/src/protected.rs
crates/decurion-hub/src/goals.rs
crates/decurion-hub/src/coordinator.rs

# The hub's database layout. A change here runs once on the owner's saved
# data and cannot simply be taken back.
crates/decurion-hub/migrations/

# What builds, checks and publishes Decurion, and which dependencies and
# licenses it accepts.
.github/workflows/
deny.toml

# The installers people download.
packaging/

# Decurion's own settings for agents, this list included.
.decurion/
